  "gaps": [
    "The capture prints only a combined 'Remaining General Education and Elective Courses 42' line for the BS in Finance. The 16-credit elective figure is derived, not printed. It assumes the 15 business core credits (WRTG 112, STAT 200, ECON 201, ECON 203, CIFS 300 or alternative) are applied to the Communications, Mathematics, Behavioral and Social Sciences, and computing slots of the 41-credit general education requirement. That leaves 26 general education credits plus 16 elective credits.",
    "Residency rules are stated only as policies, not tied to specific courses: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) must be completed at UMGC; half the credits within the major must be completed at UMGC; and at least 15 upper-level credits (300–499) must be completed at UMGC. Because of this, no individual requirement is flagged institutionalOnly.",
    "Grade and coursework rules: a minimum grade of C applies to any course used in the major. At least half the major credits must be earned through graded coursework. Pass/fail credit counts toward electives only, up to a maximum of 18 credits.",
    "The capture also contains the start of the Bachelor of Science in General Studies (27 major elective credits, 3-credit required major capstone, 41 general education credits, 49 elective credits, 120 total). It is not ledgered here. Its major elective areas and capstone course code are not included in the capture."
  ],
